GS OpenGL context: ask for 4.6, then 4.5, 4.4 and 4.3 (the shaders are GLSL 430) instead of 4.6 only. GPUs whose
drivers stop at 4.3-4.5 (Intel HD 4000-4600 on Windows, older AMD / NVIDIA) fell back to the software renderer: a
session report from an i3-4170 + Intel HD 4400 (driver 20.19.15.4531) showed 'OpenGL 4.6 core context unavailable'
and ~23 FPS. Worker contexts ask for the version the GS context got. glTextureBarrier falls back to
glTextureBarrierNV (NV_texture_barrier, same function); glBufferStorage (4.4) is optional, used only by the presented
frame's device hash. A driver that has 4.6 takes the same path as before.
GOW_GL_MAX_MINOR=<n> (test) starts at 4.n. Checked on an RX 580 with GOW_GL_MAX_MINOR=3: 4.3 context, GPU renderer
and shared presentation active, save route 57.7 FPS (57.8 with 4.6). Not yet run on an Intel HD 4400.

